! A probe at FLASH's scales, for the second machine the source filter's default is
! measured on (doc/startup-noise.md). This is not FLASH. It is a helical line whose
! wavelength, energy, current and emittance are of FLASH's order, chosen so that the
! ratio of the two angles the filter's default is built from differs from the Aramis
! benchmark's. FLASH1 itself, planar and at its published parameters, is
! examples/flash1/flash1.bmad. Nothing here is taken from a FLASH publication, and the
! numbers this file's runs produced stand as measurements of this probe.
!
! Each segment is 165 periods, so the wiggler has a whole number of them. The beam is
! ten times the emittance and five times the size of the Aramis benchmark's, the
! wavelength a hundred times longer, and z_R/L_g falls from 32 to about 14, which moves
! the ratio of the mode angle to the rho angle from 1.14 to about 1.9.
!
! The focusing. A helical undulator focuses both planes alike, and this one's natural
! strength is 8.68e-3 m^-2, which alone would hold the beta function at 10.7 m. The
! quadrupole strengths are 1.185 and -1.185 m^-2, chosen so the mean beta function over
! the cell is 10.0 m in both planes, with beta between 6.74 and 13.91 m and a phase
! advance of 66 degrees. The two halves of the cell differ only in which quadrupole they
! carry, so the vertical beta function is the horizontal one shifted by half a cell, and
! one strength sets both means.

parameter[geometry] = open
parameter[particle] = electron
parameter[e_tot] = 8.0333e8

! The matched periodic Twiss of the cell below, at the entrance of a segment. The file
! stated beta = 10 m with alpha = 0 until 2026-09-06, which is not that solution: the
! beam beat through the line at a mismatch of 2.3, its rms size swinging from 27 to
! 256 um, and every measurement made on this probe before that date was made on the
! beating beam (FINDINGS 7.56).
beginning[beta_a]  = 7.02965
beginning[alpha_a] = -0.467079
beginning[beta_b]  = 13.39578
beginning[alpha_b] = 0.768195

UND: wiggler, l = 4.5045, l_period = 0.0273, field_calc = helical_model, &
     b_max = 0.35307, tracking_method = fel_averaged, mat6_calc_method = tracking

D1: drift, l = 0.6
D2: drift, l = 0.3
QF: quadrupole, l = 0.1, k1 =  1.185
QD: quadrupole, l = 0.1, k1 = -1.185

FODO: line = (UND, D1, QF, D2, UND, D1, QD, D2)
FLASHLINE: line = (6*FODO)
use, FLASHLINE
